{ type: install
  message: <<EOM
To load intel_rapl at boot, add to /boot/loader.conf:

	intel_rapl_load="YES"

Prefer this over kld_list in /etc/rc.conf if you set any hw.intel_rapl
value in /etc/sysctl.conf: rc.d/sysctl runs before rc.d/kld, so a module
loaded from kld_list does not exist yet when those settings are applied.

Then inspect what the hardware reports:

	sysctl hw.intel_rapl

If hw.intel_rapl.locked is 1, the firmware has sealed the power limit
register and no limit can be changed from the operating system. Reads and
power measurement still work. Some BIOS setups expose a configurable TDP
option, which is then the only place to change it.

hw.intel_rapl.power_mw is a rate covering the interval since the previous
read of that same sysctl, so read it twice a few seconds apart for a figure
that means anything.
EOM
}
